    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters July 18 with a lineup headlined by three high-ceiling plays that cleared the 75-point threshold: **James Wood** (77.71), **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91), and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21). **James Wood** is our premier play today; batting lead-off against Ginn, he benefits from a strong park factor and an elite 0.437 xwOBA, proving that even against a competent arm, his profile is too potent to ignore. **Mickey Moniak** also jumps into the top tier (75.75) due to an ideal combination of park factors and a favorable platoon matchup against Lowder. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains a mandatory start (70.40) despite the SB-suppressing threat of May\u2019s pickoff ability, as his ability to contribute across all categories keeps his floor comfortably above our strong-start threshold.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Austin Riley** (52.82), who fell just shy of the efficiency requirements needed to crack the starting nine. While **Austin Riley** offers pedigree, the optimizer favored the platoon advantages of **Mickey Moniak** and the higher projected volume of **Vinnie Pasquantino** against Canning. We are keeping a close eye on **Isaac Paredes** (59.35) and **Josh Naylor** (59.20); both sit right on the border of our \"Strong\" classification. While they are slated to start, their output against Webb and Rogers, respectively, will be vital to maintaining our Roto pace. \n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, particularly regarding the basepaths. We have flagged **Corbin Carroll** and **Seiya Suzuki** for potential SB variance; **Seiya Suzuki** actually gains a minor boost (+2%) due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s delivery profile, which may open lanes for him to swipe a bag despite the tougher matchup against Bradley. Note that **Jose Caballero** is a non-factor today due to a confirmed rainout, and **Giancarlo Stanton** remains sidelined on the IL. We will monitor for any last-minute lineup adjustments for **Cole Young** and **Zach McKinstry**, who are currently holding marginal scores and could see their efficiency drop if their order positions shift further down the lineup.",
